{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:35:06Z","title":"Runtime ceiling advanced without every generated benchmark range","summary":"The P32 binding left C6 geometry benchmarks at the prior 0..=2 range, compared the maximum-Opening selector against four predicates even though four Opening predicates produce eight evaluation units, and declared 40 funding entries without populating them in the atomic benchmark. The owner was unreachable and its setup omitted one claimed maximum dimension.","scope":"actors-production-weight","status":"resolved","files":"template/pallets/actors/src/benchmarking.rs,template/runtime/src/configs/actor_config.rs,template/runtime/src/weights/pallet_deos_actors.rs","tags":"benchmark-range,configured-bound,p32,weight-soundness,unreachable-owner","remedy":"Whenever a runtime bound advances, audit every physical benchmark range and prove each special owner is selected by a realizable context whose benchmark setup and postconditions materialize every claimed maximum dimension.","related":"EXP-0010"}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T22:17:06Z","title":"Subtracting separately generated Weight owners is not a valid atomic split","summary":"A measured full-cycle Running branch had lower estimated ProofSize than the sum of separately generated queue scan/probe/consume owners because proof keys overlap. Component-wise subtraction therefore cannot derive an inner atomic owner even when RefTime subtraction appears valid.","scope":"actors-production-weight","status":"resolved","files":"template/pallets/actors/src/benchmarking.rs,template/runtime/src/configs/actor_config.rs","tags":"weight-algebra,proof-size,atomic-owner,benchmark-boundary","remedy":"Benchmark each non-overlapping ownership boundary directly. The remaining Running/Suspended and nonmaximum-Opening owners must measure the inner plan/evaluate/commit/post-placement atom after separately owned queue discovery/state loading, never derive it by subtracting independent generated estimates.","related":"I4 Control Weight Port"}
