{"timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:00:00Z","title":"Persistent funding wait solves the wrong User process-lifetime boundary","summary":"Replacing current-Step apoptosis with ActorFundingWait prevented immediate death but retained nonviable process state indefinitely and added wait authority, ingress wake, and scheduler reinsertion. It also failed the stronger invariant that an economically admitted multi-Step Cycle must finish without reclassification between Steps.","scope":"actors-user-lifecycle","status":"resolved","files":"template/pallets/actors/docs/specification.en.md,docs/actors-resource-policy.specification.en.md,.agents/skills/architecture-experiments/tracks/actors/EXP-0019.md","tags":"apoptosis,cycle-admission,funding-wait,pipeline-liveness,custody","remedy":"Evaluate User viability only while Idle. Derive a fixed-size full-Cycle economic envelope at Contract mutation, reserve retry-inclusive Cycle plus minimal-cleanup capacity at Opening, carry it through Q1, and perform custody-neutral minimal apoptosis only at a nonviable boundary.","related":"actors/EXP-0019"}
